    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5212" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bergŏmum</span></b> , i,
		n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βέργομον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a town in</i> Gallia
			Transpadana, now <i>Bergamo</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 17,
				21, § 124</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Just. 20,
				5, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
			65</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bergŏmas</span></b> , ātis,
				adj., <i>of Bergomum</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">MVNICIPIVM,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 3349</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">RESPVBLICA,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 3898</span></i>
			; and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bergomātes</span></b> , ium, m., <i>the inhabitants of Bergomum</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 17,
				21, § 125</span></i>; <i><span class="en">34, 1, 2, § 2</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Cato, Orig. 2, 4</span></i>.</div>
